      "content": "A symposium in Geneva, what a delightful setting! I can help you plan a smooth morning schedule for the opening ceremony. Let's get started, shall we?\n\nImagine a well-organized, efficient, and (dare I say it?) \"gobling\" schedule. Here's a suggested plan for Monday morning:\n\n9:00 AM - Doors Open: Welcome guests as they arrive, and have them mingle with the catering staff, who will be serving coffee and pastries. This is a great opportunity for attendees to get a feel for the venue and grab a snack before the ceremony begins.\n\n9:30 AM - Speaker Arrival and Rehearsal: Invite speakers to arrive and begin their setup. This is also a good time for the technical team to conduct a sound check and ensure everything is in working order. You might want to have a \"goblin\" of a technical assistant to double-check all the equipment, just in case.\n\n10:00 AM - Final Preparations: Take a few minutes to review the schedule, confirm the order of speakers, and make any last-minute adjustments. This is also a good time to have the catering staff finalize their setup and get everything ready for the coffee and pastries.\n\n10:15",
